Z||000007||thomas_l||09-07-2001||02:16 PM||||He could have had the same problem I did - ordered a junkyard 5-sp and got a 4-sp because the junkyard screwed up. The big clue for you is: reverse is toward you and up (4-speed) or away and back (5-speed). I think the empty space I filled with a 4-speed used to have a Getrag in it. In my case the only problem with the shifter/cables was that the shift cable was about 1/2" too short and I had to rig the shift lever (on the trans) to make it work. It was still not 100% because it liked to grind going into 3rd. The select cable worked ok. Also no back-up lights.<P>I bought some 4-speed cables from a local Fiero club member and found a shifter in a junkyard 84 4cyl and all is well now. I even got the 4-speed console sticker from Rodney Dickman and wired the back-up lights to the shifter to cover the details.||||reg||1
